WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.330 --> 00:00:01.530
<v Instructor>All right, so let's go ahead</v>

2
00:00:01.530 --> 00:00:04.500
and practice using Global Accelerator.

3
00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:06.570
So, for this, we're gonna have to create an infrastructure

4
00:00:06.570 --> 00:00:09.930
in two regions to make the Global Accelerator useful.

5
00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:10.980
But let's go ahead and create it

6
00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:13.230
and see what the options are.

7
00:00:13.230 --> 00:00:15.900
So, first of all, we need to enter an accelerator name,

8
00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:19.230
so Demo, and then an accelerator type.

9
00:00:19.230 --> 00:00:20.880
It's going to be Standard.

10
00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:24.030
Then, the routing we want is going to be IPv4

11
00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:26.073
because right now we use IPv4 addresses.

12
00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:28.440
Let's click on Next.

13
00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:29.730
And now we have listeners,

14
00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:33.150
so what do we want our accelerator to listen on?

15
00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:36.210
So the protocol is gonna be TCP,

16
00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:37.710
and the port is going to be 80

17
00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:41.610
because we're going to send HTTP traffic to our instances.

18
00:00:41.610 --> 00:00:44.310
Client affinity allows you to handle

19
00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:46.950
whether or not you want the same client

20
00:00:46.950 --> 00:00:48.780
to go to the same backend instance.

21
00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:51.360
So you can have none or have it by source IP,

22
00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:53.110
but for now we'll leave it as none.

23
00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:56.490
Let's go Next, and now we have listeners.

24
00:00:56.490 --> 00:00:59.100
So this is where you create endpoint groups

25
00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:00.330
for multiple listeners.

26
00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:02.310
So we can configure regions,

27
00:01:02.310 --> 00:01:05.400
and then we can configure instances behind the scenes.

28
00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:08.190
So, for example, here we are going to choose

29
00:01:08.190 --> 00:01:10.920
US-East-1, very nice.

30
00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:12.780
And then we add a second endpoint group,

31
00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:14.820
which is going to be EU-West-1,

32
00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:18.900
which is the region that I want to use right now.

33
00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:20.430
As you can see, for Global Accelerator,

34
00:01:20.430 --> 00:01:22.050
because it's a global service,

35
00:01:22.050 --> 00:01:24.270
on the top-hand side it says "Global".

36
00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:25.830
So that means you cannot choose any region,

37
00:01:25.830 --> 00:01:27.540
it's just a global service.

38
00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:29.520
So, here we say, "Hey, we want to send

39
00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:34.520
some traffic to US-East-1 and some traffic to US-West-1."

40
00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:36.840
You could configure port overrides and health checks,

41
00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:38.940
but no need to right now.

42
00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:40.980
Let's click on Next.

43
00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:44.640
And now we need to have endpoints in these regions.

44
00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:46.620
So right now we don't have any endpoints,

45
00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:49.890
so we cannot finish the configuration

46
00:01:49.890 --> 00:01:52.410
but let's create this accelerator.

47
00:01:52.410 --> 00:01:53.490
And while it's created,

48
00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:55.890
we're going to add endpoints afterward.

49
00:01:55.890 --> 00:01:57.360
So now endpoints are going to be,

50
00:01:57.360 --> 00:02:01.080
for example, EC2 instances or load balancers and so on.

51
00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:03.240
So, I'm going to open EC2 instances

52
00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:06.060
and first I'm going to choose US-East-1,

53
00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:09.750
which is what I want to have one of my endpoint groups in.

54
00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:13.590
And I will add an instance, and I will launch the instance.

55
00:02:13.590 --> 00:02:14.910
We're gonna go through it very quickly,

56
00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:17.283
so I'll call this one Demo Accelerator.

57
00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:23.040
We'll use the latest Amazon Linux, this is fine.

58
00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:24.930
T3 Micro, this is fine.

59
00:02:24.930 --> 00:02:26.733
We don't need a key pair.

60
00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:29.700
We can select a security group.

61
00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:31.170
Yes, we're going to create one,

62
00:02:31.170 --> 00:02:34.140
and we're going to allow HTTP traffic from the internet.

63
00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:38.160
This is going to allow our HTTP instance to be exposed.

64
00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:40.800
And then under Advanced Details

65
00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:45.540
I'm going to, at the very bottom, select my user data,

66
00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:49.890
and I'm going to choose what we had before, so this,

67
00:02:49.890 --> 00:02:52.050
but we're going to paste it in

68
00:02:52.050 --> 00:02:53.100
and we're gonna say, "Hello World

69
00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:57.090
from hostname (indistinct) in US-East-1."

70
00:02:57.090 --> 00:02:59.490
This way we know which region

71
00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:02.340
and which instance belongs to which region.

72
00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:05.700
So this is good, I'm going to just launch the instance

73
00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:06.753
and copy this again.

74
00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:11.760
So now our instance is being launched.

75
00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:14.280
Ao I'm going to do the exact same thing,

76
00:03:14.280 --> 00:03:18.870
so let's go to the instance, refresh this,

77
00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:21.993
and we're going to copy this

78
00:03:21.993 --> 00:03:23.880
IPv4 address in here and enter it.

79
00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:25.230
Right now, it's not going to work, of course,

80
00:03:25.230 --> 00:03:26.160
because it's too early,

81
00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:28.590
but at least we have the IP address ready.

82
00:03:28.590 --> 00:03:31.050
And we're going to do the exact same thing,

83
00:03:31.050 --> 00:03:35.223
but in EU-West-1, so I click on EU-West-1.

84
00:03:36.090 --> 00:03:37.640
I'm going to launch an instance

85
00:03:38.490 --> 00:03:40.777
and then call it one Demoinstance.

86
00:03:42.210 --> 00:03:47.210
Then, the same setup as before, no key pair required.

87
00:03:47.880 --> 00:03:50.523
We'll allow HTTP traffic from the internet.

88
00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:55.005
Scroll down, and we're going to paste the user data

89
00:03:55.005 --> 00:03:59.190
but this time, for the user data, which is right here,

90
00:03:59.190 --> 00:04:01.817
I'm going to have it as EU-West-1.

91
00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:07.890
All right, so now we'll have two instances.

92
00:04:07.890 --> 00:04:09.740
I'm going to launch this one as well.

93
00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:14.460
So we have two instances now that have been launched,

94
00:04:14.460 --> 00:04:18.660
one in each region, and we have two IPs

95
00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:23.660
so I'm going to open this IP address in here as well.

96
00:04:24.090 --> 00:04:26.573
So let's see for this instance if it's ready or not.

97
00:04:27.810 --> 00:04:30.840
So let's switch regions again to get back the IP

98
00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:31.863
because I lost it.

99
00:04:33.510 --> 00:04:35.043
So here's my instance.

100
00:04:36.930 --> 00:04:38.490
And, as you can see, it says, "Hello World

101
00:04:38.490 --> 00:04:41.580
from my EC2 instance in US-East-1."

102
00:04:41.580 --> 00:04:43.593
So this one has been working correctly,

103
00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:46.950
and this one is probably just a matter of time.

104
00:04:46.950 --> 00:04:49.860
Here we go, here it's, "Hello World from EU-West-1."

105
00:04:49.860 --> 00:04:52.560
So now our two instances are ready.

106
00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:55.500
And in Global Accelerator, in our accelerator,

107
00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:58.170
we're going to now configure these instances.

108
00:04:58.170 --> 00:05:02.100
So let's click on this listener,

109
00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:04.320
and we have two endpoint groups,

110
00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:07.320
one for US-East-1 and one for US-West...

111
00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:10.530
And actually, I did US-West-1 and not EU-West-1,

112
00:05:10.530 --> 00:05:14.850
so let's configure one for EU-West-1,

113
00:05:14.850 --> 00:05:16.150
which is what I wanted to.

114
00:05:17.430 --> 00:05:20.160
And now we're going to add endpoints for this EU-West-1

115
00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:22.920
and, as you can see in here, we have several options.

116
00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:25.797
So we have Application Load Balancer, Network Load Balancer,

117
00:05:25.797 --> 00:05:28.470
EC2 instance, and Elastic IP address.

118
00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:31.050
Right now, we've configured an EC2 instance,

119
00:05:31.050 --> 00:05:33.540
and we can find this instance right here.

120
00:05:33.540 --> 00:05:35.220
And the weight allows you to

121
00:05:35.220 --> 00:05:36.870
see how you want to distribute traffic

122
00:05:36.870 --> 00:05:39.120
if you had multiple endpoints.

123
00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:41.553
But this is good, we have one, we'll save it.

124
00:05:43.560 --> 00:05:47.430
Now, for this one right here, US-West-1,

125
00:05:47.430 --> 00:05:49.080
we actually don't need it so I'm going to remove it.

126
00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:50.910
This was an oversight from me.

127
00:05:50.910 --> 00:05:55.263
And for US-East-1, I'm going to click on it, add endpoints.

128
00:05:56.880 --> 00:06:01.230
And here, again, we can add our EC2 instance.

129
00:06:01.230 --> 00:06:03.963
Here we go, and click on Save.

130
00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:06.390
So now we're having issues

131
00:06:06.390 --> 00:06:09.570
with the health check setup for our EC2 instances,

132
00:06:09.570 --> 00:06:13.740
so let's go into the configuration of US-East-1.

133
00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:15.030
We're going to configure the health checks,

134
00:06:15.030 --> 00:06:18.870
and here we'll say, "Okay, check the protocol HTTP.

135
00:06:18.870 --> 00:06:22.680
The path is /, the port is 80,

136
00:06:22.680 --> 00:06:25.470
and you can have a 10-second health check interval,

137
00:06:25.470 --> 00:06:29.370
and we'll have it as two threshold count to make it faster."

138
00:06:29.370 --> 00:06:31.620
So perfect for this one.

139
00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:32.453
And we're going to configure

140
00:06:32.453 --> 00:06:35.640
the second endpoint group as well, the one for EU-West-1,

141
00:06:35.640 --> 00:06:38.940
and we'll apply the exact same thing.

142
00:06:38.940 --> 00:06:43.083
So we're going to do health checks on HTTP,

143
00:06:44.314 --> 00:06:45.660
the health check being 10 seconds,

144
00:06:45.660 --> 00:06:47.163
and the threshold being two.

145
00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:50.820
So that means we need to wait about 20 seconds

146
00:06:50.820 --> 00:06:53.220
to make sure that our endpoints are going to be healthy,

147
00:06:53.220 --> 00:06:55.170
so let's wait and I'll get back to you.

148
00:06:56.280 --> 00:06:59.100
All right, so I'm back in my Global Accelerator,

149
00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:00.420
you can get back here,

150
00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:04.110
and I had to wait for the provisioning status to be deployed

151
00:07:04.110 --> 00:07:05.370
for my health checks to pass.

152
00:07:05.370 --> 00:07:07.920
So this is why the health checks were unhealthy.

153
00:07:07.920 --> 00:07:10.110
But now that it's been provisioned

154
00:07:10.110 --> 00:07:11.940
and my health checks are passing,

155
00:07:11.940 --> 00:07:16.110
we can see that we have two static IP addresses

156
00:07:16.110 --> 00:07:18.240
available for our Global Accelerator.

157
00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:20.430
We have this one and that one.

158
00:07:20.430 --> 00:07:21.810
And so what I can do now

159
00:07:21.810 --> 00:07:24.690
is just try to use the Global Accelerator.

160
00:07:24.690 --> 00:07:27.420
So I'm going to open a URL,

161
00:07:27.420 --> 00:07:29.310
and, as you can see, by opening this IP address

162
00:07:29.310 --> 00:07:32.490
I'm redirected to my instance in EU-West-1.

163
00:07:32.490 --> 00:07:33.780
And I keep on refreshing

164
00:07:33.780 --> 00:07:36.570
